experiment: phaseteach
  phaseteach -- can a taught utterance occupy two phases of the
  creature's own free-running F1 gesture?
  the quantity  produced F1 in phase 1 minus produced F1 in phase 0
  the evidence  the DIFFERENCE between the two mappings, because the
                oscillator contributes to both equally and cancels
  refused if    the two mappings come back equal, or ph_off is not ~0,
                or ph_share is near 0 or 1 (a settled winner, not an
                alternation, and one phase bin nearly empty)


  arm           n     F1 ph0    F1 ph1  separation (ph1-ph0)    share    off  err drop (early-late)
  fixed         0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   0.00  +0.0656 +/- 0.0066  
  phase        36      616.1     635.4  +19.3 +/- 0.2 Hz         0.50   0.00  -0.0006 +/- 0.0010  
  phase-sw     36      616.0     635.3  +19.4 +/- 0.2 Hz         0.50   0.00  -0.0010 +/- 0.0009  
  fast         36      615.8     635.1  +19.3 +/- 0.2 Hz         0.50   0.00  -0.0015 +/- 0.0010  
  fast-sw      36      615.6     634.9  +19.3 +/- 0.2 Hz         0.50   0.00  -0.0014 +/- 0.0010  
  DID THE LESSON LAND     error early minus late on `fixed`, whose target does NOT
                          flip within a trial:  +0.0656 +/- 0.0066  (10.0 SE, n=36)
  CREDIT RESOLUTION  vocal tau_elig 100 ms (global 2000 x scale 0.050) against a phase of ~666 ms  ->  0.2 phases per trace
  CREDIT DELIVERY    of the credit standing at the event, the share left when the praise lands:
                      500 ms teacher    0.7%          50 ms teacher   60.7%

  THE MAPPING CONTRAST, paired on seed (identity minus swapped)
    teacher   contrast                 SE    n   credit delivered
     500 ms     -0.1 +/-   0.2 Hz     0.3   36   starved (the control)
      50 ms     -0.1 +/-   0.2 Hz     0.4   36   the ORACLE arm
  the two arms carry the SAME narrow credit window and so the same ability
  to tell the phases apart. They differ in the DELAY alone, which is the
  only axis the first run could not vary.

  NOT EVEN A FAST TEACHER REACHES THE PHASE. The two mappings are
  indistinguishable (-0.1 +/- 0.2 Hz, under 3 SE) at power to see a
  separation of 0.5 Hz, with a credit window inside one phase and a
  teacher fast enough to deliver it. The phase difference in the table is
  the OSCILLATOR and reward has no purchase on it.

  THIS IS THE RESULT THE RUN WAS BUILT TO GET. The delay was the last
  free parameter: resolution and delivery are both satisfied here and the
  lesson still cannot aim the gesture. So the gap is not the credit
  PATHWAY, and building a delay line or a synaptic tag would buy nothing --
  the cheap oracle refuses the expensive build, which is what it was for.
  What is left is that reward reaches the vocal module as a quantity with
  no phase-specific target to write INTO; see the axis-collision line.
